<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">A Catholic publishing house · St. Louis · Since 2014</p>
      <h1>Make the time.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Nearly 700 books in theology, philosophy, spirituality, literature, poetry, and children's stories, from scholars, clergy, poets, and first-time authors. Published to be read, not warehoused.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/books/">Browse the books</a><a class="btn ghost" href="/submissions/">Submit a manuscript</a></div>
      <form class="search-bar" action="/books/" method="get" style="margin-top:1.6rem"><input type="search" name="q" placeholder="Search by title or author" aria-label="Search books"><button class="btn brass" type="submit">Search</button></form>
    </div>
    <div class="shelf">
    {%- for b in books | recent(3) %}<a href="/books/{{ b.slug }}/"><img src="{{ b.cover }}" alt="{{ b.title }}" onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='/images/cover-coming-soon.jpg'" width="400" height="600"{% if loop.first %} fetchpriority="high"{% else %} loading="lazy"{% endif %}></a>{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head"><h2>Featured</h2><p class="band-note">{{ featured.intro }}</p></div>
    <div class="books featured">
    {%- for slug in featured.featured %}{% for b in books %}{% if b.slug == slug %}{% include "bookcard.njk" %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band white">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head"><h2>Award winners</h2><a class="textlink" href="/awards/">All awards →</a></div>
    <div class="award-row">
    {%- for a in featured.awards.slice(0, 6) %}{% for b in books %}{% if b.slug == a.slug %}
      <a class="award-card" href="/books/{{ b.slug }}/"><img src="{{ b.cover }}" alt="" onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='/images/cover-coming-soon.jpg'" loading="lazy" width="400" height="600"><span><strong>{{ b.title }}</strong><em>{{ a.award }}</em></span></a>
    {%- endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band paper-2">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <img src="/images/home-PC-Enroute-Advertising-Book-Framed.jpg" alt="Mater Ecclesiae: Mother of the Church, by Joseph P. Michael" width="918" height="1257" loading="lazy" style="max-width:360px;justify-self:center">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Introducing</p>
      <h2>Mater Ecclesiae: Mother of the Church</h2>
      <p class="lede">By Joseph P. Michael. The first volume of Apologia Pro Sancta Maria, on Mary as Mother of Fair Love and Mother of the Church.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/books/motherofthechurch/">See the book</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band white">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head"><h2>Author collections</h2></div>
    <div class="collections">
    {%- for c in authorsets.collections %}
      <a class="collection" href="/collections/{{ c.slug }}/"><img src="{{ c.banner }}" alt="{{ c.name }}" loading="lazy"><span><strong>{{ c.name }}</strong><em>{{ c.tagline }}</em></span></a>
    {%- endfor %}
      <a class="collection text" href="/category/deacon-james-keating-collection/"><span><strong>Deacon James Keating Collection</strong><em>Five books on the spiritual life and priestly formation.</em></span></a>
      <a class="collection text" href="/category/dianne-ahern-collection/"><span><strong>Dianne Ahern Collection</strong><em>Nine books for children on the sacraments and the saints.</em></span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap two-col top">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">News</p>
      <h2>En Route, now on groundwood.</h2>
      <p>En Route is now offering groundwood paper for its eligible paperback titles, especially novels and other text-heavy works. Beyond its environmental benefits, groundwood offers a richer, more tactile reading experience: higher opacity, less glare, and the textured feel readers associate with classic trade paperbacks. The pages turn more easily and the book reads warmer. Groundwood books generate at least 15 percent fewer carbon emissions than standard paper while keeping excellent readability and print quality. Titles with heavy ink coverage will continue to use cream or white paper where needed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="quote-card">
      <p class="kicker">From the American Academy of Distance Learning</p>
      <blockquote class="pull">"Two contemporary examples are St. Augustine's Press founded by Bruce Fingerhut, and En Route Books founded by Sebastian Mahfood and Ronda Chervin... these two individuals are the lone defenders of the civilization, culture and philosophical and theological truths of 'the West.'"</blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head"><h2>New this season</h2><a class="textlink" href="/books/">All {{ books.length }} titles →</a></div>
    <div class="books">
    {%- for b in books | recent(10) %}{% include "bookcard.njk" %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band white">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head"><h2>Browse by subject</h2></div>
    <div class="cats">
    {%- for c in categories %}<a href="/category/{{ c.slug }}/">{{ c.name }}<span>{{ c.count }}</span></a>{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band harbor">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker" style="color:var(--brass-2)">Our model</p>
      <h2>Mission over scale.</h2>
      <p class="lede">En Route is a traditional publisher on a print-on-demand model. No warehouses, no large print runs, no author fees. We assume the cost of preparing a book for publication; authors earn a 10 percent royalty on retail sales and buy copies at a 40 percent discount.</p>
      <p>That model lets us publish voices a larger house would pass over: a retired deacon's spiritual direction, a scientist's case for faith, a first novel, a book of poems. Since 2014, nearly 700 of them. Eligible paperbacks now print on groundwood paper, the richer, more tactile stock of a bookshop paperback.</p>
      <a class="textlink" href="/about/">How we work →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="steps" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.2)">
      <div><h3>Submit</h3><p>A complete, professionally edited manuscript in Word, with a cover page.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Prepare</h3><p>We design, typeset, and prepare the book for print and Kindle at our cost.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Publish</h3><p>Paperback, often hardback, Kindle, and where it fits, Audible.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Reach</h3><p>Distribution through Amazon and wholesale, and a seat on WCAT Radio.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band white">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head"><h2>{{ videos.heading }}</h2><p class="band-note">{{ videos.intro }}</p></div>
    <div class="videos">
    {%- for v in videos.items %}
      <figure class="video">
        <div class="vframe"><iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/{{ v.id }}" title="{{ v.title }}" loading="lazy" allowfullscreen allow="accelerometer; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture"></iframe></div>
        <figcaption><strong>{{ v.title }}</strong>{% if v.note %}<span>{{ v.note }}</span>{% endif %}</figcaption>
      </figure>
    {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <img src="/images/header.jpg" alt="Driftwood on a beach, En Route's motto: Make the time" width="1920" height="900" loading="lazy">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">WCAT Radio and TV</p>
      <h2>Over a hundred programs. Thousands of episodes.</h2>
      <p>Since 2016 En Route's authors have had a second home on WCAT Radio, a Catholic internet radio station with more than a hundred programs and thousands of podcast episodes, and on WCAT TV. Publish with us and your book gets heard as well as read.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/radio/">About WCAT</a><a class="btn ghost" href="{{ site.wcat }}">Listen now</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band white">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Faith and science</p>
      <h2>ITEST: where theology meets the lab.</h2>
      <p>The Institute for Theological Encounter with Science and Technology is an association of theologians, scientists, clergy, and teachers committed to a Catholic world view in which faith and science collaborate in exploring the truth. Begun in 1966 by Fr. Robert Brungs, SJ, a physicist, and Dr. John Matschiner, a biochemist, and now directed by Sebastian Mahfood, ITEST publishes a quarterly journal, runs a webinar series on WCAT Radio, and produces Creation Lens, a faith-and-science program for elementary schools. En Route publishes its books.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="https://faithscience.org/">Visit ITEST</a><a class="btn ghost" href="https://wcatradio.com/itest/">ITEST webinars</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="facts">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0">ITEST in brief</h3>
      <dl>
        <dt>Founded</dt><dd>1966 (incorporated 1968), St. Louis</dd>
        <dt>Director</dt><dd>Sebastian Mahfood, OP</dd>
        <dt>Journal</dt><dd>The quarterly ITEST Bulletin</dd>
        <dt>Webinars</dt><dd>Series running since November 2019</dd>
        <dt>For schools</dt><dd>Creation Lens: Exploring the World, Discovering God</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band white">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head"><h2>Recognition</h2></div>
    <div class="recog-cards">
      <div><img class="recog-logo" src="/images/logo-acp.png" alt="Association of Catholic Publishers" loading="lazy"><p class="kicker">Member</p><h3>Association of Catholic Publishers</h3><p>The trade association of Catholic publishing houses in North America.</p></div>
      <div><svg class="recog-logo seal" viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="2019 St. Louis Award, Publisher"><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="56" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="48" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/><text x="60" y="54" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Crimson Pro, Georgia, serif" font-size="34" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">2019</text><text x="60" y="72" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Karla, sans-serif" font-size="9" letter-spacing="1.5" fill="currentColor">ST. LOUIS AWARD</text><text x="60" y="86" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Karla, sans-serif" font-size="9" letter-spacing="2" fill="currentColor">PUBLISHER</text></svg><p class="kicker">2019</p><h3>St. Louis Award, Publisher</h3><p>Named St. Louis's publisher of the year.</p></div>
      <div><svg class="recog-logo quote" viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="56" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><text x="60" y="130" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Crimson Pro, Georgia, serif" font-size="100" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">&#8220;</text></svg><p class="kicker">Recognized by</p><h3>American Academy of Distance Learning</h3><p>Cited alongside St. Augustine's Press as a house that publishes what larger presses will not.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

